---
alwaysApply: true
globs: *.vue,*.tsx,*.ts
---

For most CSS styles, utilize [UnoCSS Attributify mode](https://unocss.dev/presets/attributify) whenever ssible to apply styles, aiming to improve code cleanliness.

Prefer use the UnoCSS Attributify mode, especially in the following cases:

1. `flex="~ col 1 items-center justify-between"`: Flex-related utilities.
2. `grid="~ cols-1 lg:cols-3 gap-4"`: Grid-related utilities.
3. `un-text="sm zinc-600 dark:zinc-400"`: Text-related utilities. Use the `un-text` attribute name to avoid conflicts, as `text` is a common prop.
4. `border="2 rounded blue-200"`: Border-related utilities.
5. `p="y2 x4"`, `m="y2 x4"`: Padding and margin-related utilities. If applying to a single axis only, use syntax like `px="2"` or `mx="2"`.
6. `bg="zinc-400 dark:zinc-600"`: Background-related utilities. If setting gradients, it is best to apply them directly within the `class` attribute or use individual attribute values.

For those only one attributes utility, can be valueless attributes. For example,

```html
<div class="m-2 rounded text-teal-400" />
```

now can be

```html
<div m-2 rounded text-teal-400 />
```
